      "writtenOn": "2022-04-15T09:33:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is generally not recommended to bind to specific ports in tests because if something else happens to be using the same port, the test will fail. This makes the test flaky. It\u0027s particularly true for TCP because sockets keep the port open for a while after they are closed.\n\nInstead, suggest binding to 0 and then using getLocalAddress() to get the port. That ensures that the socket will always be bound (well, unless the whole device runs out of ports :-)).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 71,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "743eb64a02df0b27ee3d3123eaac3cb22fefbac7",
